{"header":{"status":{"name":"Success","code":0,"description":"Query success","apiHelp":"https://www.censtatd.gov.hk/en/web_table.html?id=315-37002&api_popup=1"},"title":"BoP as a ratio to Gross Domestic Product (GDP)","tablenote":["In the current account, exports of goods and services and primary income inflows are credit entries, while imports of goods and services and primary income outflows are debit entries. The balance figure in the current account is obtained by subtracting debit entries from credit entries. A positive value for the balance figure represents a surplus whereas a negative value represents a deficit.     A new sign convention has been adopted for the entire series of the financial account since June 2023. From then on, an increase in net assets (net financial outflow) is indicated by a positive value while a decrease in net assets (net financial inflow) is indicated by a negative value.","@ Figure is subject to revision later on."],"source":"Balance of Payments Branch (1),  Census and Statistics Department  (Enquiry telephone no. : 3863 2329  Enquiry e-mail : bop@censtatd.gov.hk)","count":{"noOfRecords":38,"started":"2026-10-20T20:02:02+00:00","finished":"2026-10-20T20:02:02+00:00","durationSeconds":0.05128}},"dataSet":[{"BOP_COMPONENT":"BOP_C","BOP_COMPONENTDesc":"Overall Balance of Payments","freq":"Y","period":"1998","sv":"RGDP","svDesc":"% to GDP","figure":-3.1,"sd_value":""},{"BOP_COMPONENT":"CRA","BOP_COMPONENTDesc":"Current account","freq":"Y","period":"1998","sv":"RGDP","svDesc":"% to GDP","figure":1.7,"sd_value":""},{"BOP_COMPONENT":"FNRA","BOP_COMPONENTDesc":"Financial non-reserve assets","freq":"Y","period":"1998","sv":"RGDP","svDesc":"% to GDP","figure":3.9,"sd_value":""},{"BOP_COMPONENT":"GS","BOP_COMPONENTDesc":"Goods and services","freq":"Y","period":"1998","sv":"RGDP","svDesc":"% to GDP","figure":0.5,"sd_value":""},{"BOP_COMPONENT":"GSC","BOP_COMPONENTDesc":"Credit","freq":"Y","period":"1998","sv":"RGDP","svDesc":"% to GDP","figur